<h1>Where md4c parses differently from the parser before it</h1>
<p>Each case below rendered differently before the switch to md4c (#195); the golden file pins how it
renders now. The pull request lists what each one did before.</p>
<h2>A table after a paragraph line</h2>
<p>Results:
| a | b |
|---|---|
| 1 | 2 |</p>
<h2>A delimiter row with fewer cells than the header</h2>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>one</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>x</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h2>A table ends only at a blank line</h2>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>a</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>1</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>## heading after the table</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h2>A pipe in a code span in a table cell</h2>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>command</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>ls | wc -l</code></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h2>Single tildes inside a word</h2>
<p>H~2~O and E=mc~2~</p>
<h2>Indented HTML after a paragraph</h2>
<p>para</p>
    <div>indented four</div>
<h2>A thematic break after a reference definition</h2>
<hr />
<h2>Looseness after an HTML block in an item</h2>
<ul>
<li>
<div>
html
</div>
</li>
<li>item</li>
<li>item two</li>
</ul>
<h2>An item that starts with indented code</h2>
<ol>
<li>
<pre><code>code
</code></pre>
para</li>
</ol>
<h2>A reference definition then a list in an item</h2>
<ul>
<li>
<ul>
<li>nested</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<h2>Continuation lines keep no indentation</h2>
<ol>
<li>
<h2>heading</h2>
<p>back<br />
slash</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h2>Backticks: a long run that never closes</h2>
<p>````````` x <code>code one</code>, <code>.</code>, more <code>code two</code>; <code>x</code> end</p>
<h2>An empty task item</h2>
<ul>
<li><input disabled="" type="checkbox"></li>
<li><input checked="" disabled="" type="checkbox"> done</li>
</ul>
